---
description: Run gh with unsandboxed shell so macOS keychain tokens work
alwaysApply: true
---

# GitHub CLI (`gh`) in agent shells

On macOS, `gh` stores credentials in the system keychain. Sandboxed agent shells
cannot read that keychain, so `gh auth status` / `gh run` / `gh api` fail with
"token in keyring is invalid" or HTTP `Forbidden` even when the user is logged in.

## Required

- When running any `gh` command that needs auth (status, api, run, pr, issue,
  release, workflow, etc.), use the Shell tool with `required_permissions: ["all"]`.
- Quote URLs that contain `?` so zsh does not glob them, e.g.
  `gh api 'repos/owner/repo/actions/runs?per_page=5'`.

## Do not

- Treat sandbox `Forbidden` / "invalid keyring token" as a need to re-login or
  rotate PATs until the same command has been retried unsandboxed.
- Paste PATs into the transcript unless the user explicitly provides one for
  `gh auth login --with-token`.
